{"author":{"id":"40e3ba2788b3b9fc163c354afc44e5f9d225bcf0a27e679aaa878dd6135c6dcb"},"ops":[{"type":6,"timestamp":1795229813,"nonce":"vsc+0aSFgo3j/kcWFuQE1HcR8Ws=","target":"382f4cb0da45e4dfec960aa2273809ef77d1cb896cf6fed6480ba1ccf1f5f4d0","message":"Observed during alpha13 verification; separate from the completed transactional-output changes. (1) create_archive derives the stored root for a dot input using narrow getcwd, so a non-ASCII current-directory basename can still be misinterpreted on Windows with a non-UTF-8 ANSI code page. wmain now fixes explicit command-line argument conversion, not that OS-supplied name. The legacy uc2_ingest_restore pathname also goes through the library narrow fopen and needs a separate Unicode-path audit. (2) A local MinGW 15.1 cross-build with CPATH unset fails in pre-existing compatibility headers: mode_t/S_ISDIR/getcwd aliases are missing under NO_OLDNAMES, and compat_win32.c uses DIR fields from the MSVC replacement header while MinGW provides a different layout. Native MSVC builds/tests pass; no MinGW release binary is published. Reproduce and address these paths in a focused portability change with native/cross-build tests.","files":null}]}